Caemble reimplements the published low-pass filter, region-based generator
torque curve, gain-scheduled collective pitch PI control, and command limits in
readable Python. The implementation accepts explicit Catalog parameters instead
of embedded turbine constants, uses SI arrays rather than the Bladed DLL swap
interface, and stores task-scoped checkpoint state for repeated coupling trials.
It does not include or execute the original Fortran controller during native
Solver operation. These implementation and interface changes were made in 2026.

